=== REASONING ===
  Chosen approach: a self-contained, model-driven SwiftUI surface `Drawer(model:)` that
    reproduces the web component's composition + behaviour (edge-anchored sliding glass
    panel over a tap-to-dismiss scrim; titled header with close; scrollable body; footer)
    AND hosts a representative data-bound body so EVERY prompt-required state renders INSIDE
    the panel — loading (skeleton rows), empty (ContentUnavailableView), error (retry),
    stale (chip + banner + ONE auto-refresh), offline (cached body + chip), content
    (label/value rows). Binding flows through a `DrawerSource` seam (P1/S8); the view never
    networks. Dismissal (web `onClose`) is one path shared by the scrim tap, the close
    button, the footer Done, the Escape keyboard shortcut (.cancelAction), and the VoiceOver
    escape action. Presentation marks the panel .isModal and moves VoiceOver focus onto it
    (web "focus the first focusable"). Motion honours Reduce Motion (web spring -> native
    spring, degrading to a fade).
  Rejected: (a) porting the web Tailwind/framer-motion literally — replaced with platform
    materials + tokens + a native spring/transition per HIG; (b) re-using/redeclaring the
    atomic `tsDrawer`/`TSDrawerEdge` (out of scope + a name collision) — the surface composes
    its own chrome; (c) a generic `Drawer<Content,Footer>` with no model — it could not
    satisfy the prompt's mandatory loading/empty/error/stale/offline states (the web
    container delegates those to its children), so the surface binds a `DrawerModel` that
    drives them, the same way the merged sibling surfaces widen a web content/empty split
    into the full envelope.
  Disposition vs project wiring: the merged siblings in THIS tree (ReauthDialog 0007,
    SessionExpiringModal 0009, JobProgressDrawer 0005) ship ONLY their per-surface files and
    do NOT edit project.yml / .swiftlint.yml (parallel-unsafe + outside the prompt's "Allowed
    files"). This surface follows that exact disposition: 10 files under
    apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/Drawer.* + this log, nothing else. Integration into
    the app target's source list happens at the acceptance-gate integration step, as for the
    siblings. The surface is verified to compile + test against the REAL design system in
    isolation, and proven collision-free against the whole app target (below).

